/* =========================================================================
   Selection of a Neuromuscular Blocking Agent for Rapid Sequence
   Induction and Intubation — Succinylcholine vs Rocuronium — content data.

   The algorithm (NODES: label / sub) is transcribed, box for box, from
   Figure 1 of the authors' own systematic review manuscript ("Succinylcholine
   versus Rocuronium for Tracheal Intubation: A Systematic Review of
   Intubating Conditions, Procedural Ease and Clinical Outcomes"). The
   manuscript itself was condensed by Gemini before being handed to this
   tool (see tools/gemini-condensation-prompt.md v2 in the hub repo); the
   figure's own box text was independently cross-checked against the
   original TIFF image, not taken from the condensation alone.

   Unlike this atlas's earlier author-directed-exception tools, EVERY
   reference below was independently re-resolved against a primary source
   (DOI resolution, PubMed/PMC, or an independent citing source) rather
   than accepted on the manuscript's word — this is the atlas's standard,
   full-verification methodology, with no exception granted for this tool.
   See the `kind` field on each reference for exactly what was confirmed,
   and README.md's Status section for anything flagged during that pass.

   One reference gap could not be resolved from the materials available:
   the manuscript's own narrative text cites a range "[92-98]" in two
   places, implying a reference #98, but the condensed reference list
   stops at #97. This is flagged in README.md rather than invented.

   Rendering note: the figure's closing "APPLIES TO EVERY PATHWAY" pearls
   box sits visually apart from the decision tree, with no arrow in or out
   of it in the original image — preserved here by giving that node no
   entry in EDGES at all (see app.js).
   ========================================================================= */

